{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בהנחל", :translit "b'hanchil", :gloss "when He bequeaths"} {:he "כל שהוא", :translit "kol shehu", :gloss "anything at all"} {:he "ובנו", :translit "uv'no", :gloss "and his son"} {:he "ובן בנו", :translit "uven b'no", :gloss "and his son's son"} {:he "ת\"ח", :translit "tach", :gloss "etc."} {:he "הרי היא לו כנחלה שאין לו הפסק", :translit "harei hi lo k'nachlah she'ein lo hefsek", :gloss "behold it is to him like an inheritance that has no interruption"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Talmudic legal formula listing inheritors applied to the verse's language of bequeathal"}], :frame {:text "The laws of inheritance define a chain of heirs: a man's property passes to his son, then his son's son, and so on in perpetuity. This succession is codified in Mishnah Bava Batra 8:1, which opens the list of heirs with 'his son and his son's son,' and is elaborated in Bava Batra 108a.", :sources ["Mishnah Bava Batra 8:1" "Bava Batra 108a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "גבלת", :translit "g'vulat", :gloss "He set boundaries"} {:he "חסר ווי\"ן", :translit "chaser vavim", :gloss "deficient of vavs"} {:he "י\"ב מזלות", :translit "yud-bet mazalot", :gloss "12 constellations"} {:he "יצב למספר בני ישראל", :translit "yatziyv l'mispar b'nei yisrael", :gloss "He established corresponding to the number of the children of Israel"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "גבלת חסר ווי\"ן", :b "י\"ב מזלות"}], :frame {:text "The tradition that God established twelve constellations corresponding to the twelve tribes of Israel appears in midrashic sources. Bereshit Rabbah 65:9 links the twelve tribes to the twelve signs of the zodiac, and Shabbat 156a discusses the twelve mazalot and their celestial governance.", :sources ["Bereshit Rabbah 65:9" "Shabbat 156a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Talmudic legal formula listing inheritors applied to the verse's language of bequeathal", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "גבלת חסר ווי\"ן", :a-value 775, :b "י\"ב מזלות", :b-value 495, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:53.006178592Z", :model "glm-5.2"}